      "diagnosticFeatures": [
        "Thick cylindrical marine polychaete up to 15-25 cm long with clearly differentiated thoracic, abdominal, and tail regions.",
        "Middle abdominal segments bear 13 pairs of bushy, vascularized external branchial gills (branchiae).",
        "Head lacks eyes and tentacles; eversible muscular papillose proboscis used for sediment ingestion and burrowing.",
        "Body segments subdivided by secondary external annuli; parapodia reduced with capillary chaetae and hooked uncini."
      ],
      "description": "Arenicola marina is the classic marine lugworm of intertidal sand flats. Lives in J-shaped or U-shaped burrows leaving characteristic spiral sand castings.",
