        "Elongated, dorsoventrally flattened body consisting of 21-23 trunk segments, each bearing a single pair of walking legs.",
        "First pair of trunk appendages modified into powerful, claw-like forcipules (toxicognaths) containing venom glands.",
        "Legs are bright yellow to orange-yellow contrasting against a dark reddish-maroon or brownish tergite body.",
        "Terminal legs elongated with sharp spines, used for gripping prey or hanging upside down in cave ceilings."
