    "morphology": {
      "diagnosticFeatures": [
        "Cylindrical, soft gelatinous vase-like body up to 10-15 cm in height, permanently attached at base.",
        "Covered by a transparent, flexible tunic composed of tunicin (a structural polysaccharide identical to plant cellulose).",
        "Terminal apical oral incurrent siphon and slightly sub-terminal atrial excurrent siphon with yellow-bordered margins.",
        "Expansive pharyngeal basket with thousands of ciliated stigmata and a ventral iodinated endostyle.",
        "Free-swimming tadpole larva exhibits full chordate hallmarks (notochord, dorsal nerve cord, post-anal tail), resorbed during metamorphosis."
      ],
      "description": "Ciona intestinalis is the world-famous vase tunicate. Solitary ascidian sea squirt and a premier model organism in chordate developmental genetics.",
      "maxStandardLengthCm": 15,
      "coloration": "Translucent greenish-yellow with bright yellow siphon rims spotted with red."
    },
